### 7. Real-World Impact
Markov Chain models can be applied to:
- Weather Prediction
- Population Dynamics
- Queueing Theory
- Service and Reliability Systems
- Stochastic Decision-Making

### 8. Limitations & Assumptions
- Transition probabilities remain constant.
- The model uses only three weather states.
- The next day's weather depends only on the current state.
- Real-world weather is more complex than this simplified model.

### 9. Future Scope
- Real-time Weather API Integration
- More Weather States and Historical Data
- Comparison with Actual Weather Observations
- Interactive Web Dashboard
- Extension to Population and Queueing Models

